Building from upstream source
==============================

This package must be built from the official PyPI source tarball, not directly
from a git checkout. The upstream "make package" target builds JavaScript/CSS
assets via npm before creating the sdist. These pre-built assets live in
src/oscar/static/ and are included in the distribution tarball via MANIFEST.in.

A raw git checkout will have an empty src/oscar/static/ directory, causing
the admin dashboard to be missing styles and interactive features.

Downloading upstream releases
------------------------------

Use uscan (from devscripts) to check for new releases:

    uscan --no-download          # just check what's available
    uscan                        # download the latest release automatically

Or manually fetch a specific version from pypi.debian.net:

    wget https://pypi.debian.net/django-oscar/django_oscar-4.2.tar.gz \
         -O django-oscar_4.2.orig.tar.gz

Building the package
---------------------

    dpkg-source -x django-oscar_*.dsc
    cd django-oscar-*/
    dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc

No npm or nodejs is required at build time — all assets are pre-built in
the upstream tarball. Two quilt patches are applied:

  debian/patches/1001-use-local-jquery.patch
    Replaces the Google CDN jQuery reference with the bundled local copy,
    eliminating an external network dependency and a lintian error.

  debian/patches/2001-remove-npm-build.patch
    Removes the BuildNPM class from setup.py which would otherwise try to run npm.
